            "content": "Videofluoroscopic Swallowing Study (VFSS), also called modified barium swallow (MBS), is the gold standard for evaluating oropharyngeal dysphagia. Key indications include: suspected aspiration, unexplained dysphagia, recurrent pneumonia, weight loss due to swallowing difficulty, sensation of food sticking in throat, and post-surgical/neurological swallowing assessment. VFSS provides real-time fluoroscopic imaging of all phases of swallowing (oral preparatory, oral propulsive, pharyngeal, and upper esophageal) using radio-opaque contrast. It uniquely demonstrates: timing and coordination of swallowing structures, bolus flow dynamics, presence and timing of aspiration (before/during/after swallow), penetration into the laryngeal vestibule, residue location and amount, and effectiveness of compensatory strategies.",
